From fd5cd6a3c707781d29f6fe825ccdb6e2315399c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:23:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 32/36] [AGS] Fix five more
 int32_t/uint32_t-vs-int/unsigned-int sites in Common/

Same established DJGPP ILP32 divergence as patches 0013/0018/0019/0024/0027
(int32_t is long int, uint32_t is unsigned long -- distinct types from
int/unsigned int here, even though all are 4 bytes, unlike a 64-bit
host where int32_t/uint32_t collapse to int/unsigned int) -- but found
in a genuinely new way this time: a full cmake --build build/ags -j$(nproc)
-- -k pass after patch 0031 reached COMPILES's Engine-side blocker
(ali3dsw.cpp/gfxfilter_sdl_renderer.cpp) but then failed inside Common/
on five files that turned out to have never actually been compiled by
any prior session's build at all -- confirmed by comparing Common/'s own
.obj count against its .cpp count (68 of 91) before this patch: these
five files' real compile errors were latent, not introduced by anything
in this session, just never reached until a CMakeLists.txt edit forced
a full reconfigure that invalidated the stale, partial object cache.

- Common/ac/gamesetupstruct.cpp (2 sites), Common/data/tra_file.cpp
  (1 site): std::max(0, in->ReadInt32()) -- ambiguous template deduction
  between int and int32_t. FontInfo::LineSpacing (gamestructdefines.h) is
  a plain int, so cast ReadInt32()'s result down to int to match, rather
  than the other way around.
- Common/gfx/allegrobitmap.h: Bitmap::RotateBlt's two declarations said
  plain "int angle"; both real definitions (allegrobitmap.cpp) already
  used fixed_t (int32_t, platform/types.h) -- fixed_t is also the
  semantically correct type here (a fixed-point angle), so the
  declarations are fixed to match the definitions, not the reverse (same
  choice patch 0018 made for cc_serializer's override mismatch).
- Common/gfx/image_png.cpp: palette_colors was declared uint32_t[PAL_SIZE]
  but passed to the vendored stb_image.h's own
  stbi_load_from_callbacks_with_palette(..., unsigned int *palette_buffer, ...)
  -- a pointer-type mismatch, not just a value-level ambiguity, so no
  cast suffices; changed the local array's element type to unsigned int
  instead (still exactly 4 bytes under DJGPP, so the later
  reinterpret_cast<uint8_t*> byte-level read of r/g/b/a per entry is
  unaffected).
- Engine/ac/display.h: wouttext_aligned's 8-arg declaration said "int
  outline_color"; its real definition (display.cpp) and its sibling
  wouttext_outline's declaration one line above both already use
  color_t (int32_t) -- fixed the declaration to match, an isolated typo
  relative to its own neighboring declarations, not a systemic gap in
  this specific file.

Verified: all five files compile clean in the same full build that
reached COMPILES (see the two patches immediately following this one
for the remaining link-time gaps that same build surfaced).
---
 Common/ac/gamesetupstruct.cpp |  9 +++++++--
 Common/data/tra_file.cpp      |  7 ++++++-
 Common/gfx/allegrobitmap.h    | 10 ++++++++--
 Common/gfx/image_png.cpp      |  9 ++++++++-
 Engine/ac/display.h           |  7 ++++++-
 5 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Common/ac/gamesetupstruct.cpp b/Common/ac/gamesetupstruct.cpp
index ed87f0466..c3d3d6009 100644
--- a/Common/ac/gamesetupstruct.cpp
+++ b/Common/ac/gamesetupstruct.cpp
@@ -81,7 +81,12 @@ void GameSetupStruct::read_font_infos(Common::Stream *in, GameDataVersion data_v
         {
             fonts[i].YOffset = in->ReadInt32();
             if (data_ver >= kGameVersion_341_2)
-                fonts[i].LineSpacing = std::max(0, in->ReadInt32());
+                // DOS-PORT: std::max(int, int32_t) is ambiguous under DJGPP's
+                // ILP32 model (int32_t is long int, distinct from int) --
+                // same divergence as patches 0013/0018/0019/0024/0027;
+                // LineSpacing is a plain int (gamestructdefines.h), so cast
+                // to match it rather than the other way around.
+                fonts[i].LineSpacing = std::max(0, (int)in->ReadInt32());
         }
     }
     else
@@ -93,7 +98,7 @@ void GameSetupStruct::read_font_infos(Common::Stream *in, GameDataVersion data_v
             fonts[i].Size = in->ReadInt32();
             fonts[i].Outline = in->ReadInt32();
             fonts[i].YOffset = in->ReadInt32();
-            fonts[i].LineSpacing = std::max(0, in->ReadInt32());
+            fonts[i].LineSpacing = std::max(0, (int)in->ReadInt32());
             fonts[i].SetFlags(flags);
         }
     }
